From e0df60b6bedfba33fd0677b5b75d7486d8adaa46 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: coderxp1 <327264955+coderxp1@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 17:40:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Runtime slice: real per-agent PTY sessions behind enforced
 authorization

Implements the smallest real vertical slice: one disposable agent session
end-to-end (plus a second for isolation) with a real persistent PTY per
agent, structured argv dispatch, approval-gated shell-script capability,
live labelled streaming, control leases, reconnect-by-cursor with bounded
retention and gap notices, op-ID reconciliation, timeout/cancel with
verified descendant cleanup, fail-closed health, and workspace persistence
across runtime replacement.

Authorization (tightened, still separate from PR #1): approvals bind the
complete normalized operation (actor, project, session, action, args hash,
resource, network scope, exec mode, destination, revision, protected flag,
op ID, issuer epoch, expiry); shell-script exec is approval-only, never
grant-covered; issuer epochs invalidate pre-restart approvals; missing or
throwing authorization dependencies fail closed with
AUTHORIZATION_UNAVAILABLE (503). runtime.allocate uses first-claim
ownership; every dispatch re-verifies request-equals-authorized-operation.

Isolation per session: unprivileged host uid, no-egress network namespace
(unshare -U -n -r), prlimit caps, scrubbed environment, structural
per-owner workspace confinement. No general egress offered.

Sanitizer: strict UTF-8 byte caps (notice inside budget), surrogate-safe
cuts, chunk-split secret redaction incl. underscore token prefixes, and
honest success reporting (no exit-0/running/port-3000/stopped
fabrications).

Tests wired into npm test: test-action-authorization (17 sections),
test-sanitizer-bytes (6), test-agent-runtime-authz (12). Live smoke
(smoke-agent-runtime-live.ts, 32 checks) stays out of the aggregate suite.

Iteration evidence only: Node v22 + locally rebuilt node-pty. Supported-
runtime (Node 24) build evidence still requires the pinned artifact.

